    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That sounds a bit vague for a USPTO response. \"Geometrical complexity\" and \"improved thermal efficiency\" are pretty standard claims that examiners see all the time. \n\nIf I'm being honest, looking at the actual specs for the 2018 patent, the lattice structures are fundamentally the same type of architecture. If we try to push \"complexity\" as the main differentiator without a concrete technical delta, we're going to get rejected for obviousness. \n\nIs there anything in the AeroFlow specs that *actually* provides a structural or chemical difference, or are we just trying to frame a similar technology as something new to get them their funding?",
      "source": "evaluator"
